cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IOsonata in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "0.13"
date-released: 2026-11-01
title: "IOsonata: bare-metal, event-driven C++ HAL and firmware framework for microcontrollers"
abstract: >-
  IOsonata is an open-source, bare-metal C++ hardware-abstraction layer,
  device-driver library and event-driven firmware framework for
  microcontrollers. It uses object-oriented design with runtime polymorphism,
  ships one precompiled static library per MCU, and includes a Bluetooth LE
  host, a composable USB device stack, NVM storage, crypto, and sensor and
  display drivers. Hardware results are recorded for Nordic nRF52, nRF53,
  nRF54L and nRF91, STM32F0, L4, G4, H7 and WBA, Renesas RA4M1, Microchip
  SAM4L and SAM D, and NXP LPC54628 parts; the repository also contains
  ports for other Nordic, STM32, Renesas, NXP and RISC-V MCUs.
